<title>FRANCE: CDC stake in Accor down to 9.76 pct -CMF.</title>
<headline>CDC stake in Accor down to 9.76 pct -CMF.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>French state-owned bank Caisse des Depots et Consignation's holding in Accor fell to 9.76 percent of the voting rights on June 16 following a sale of shares on the market, the CMF markets supervisory body said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The CMF issued a statement notifying the change due to the drop below a 10 percent threshold.</p>
<p>The bank held 11.71 percent of the capital and 13.64 percent of the voting rights in hotels group Accor at the end of 1996, according to Accor's annual report.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
